repository-code: "https://github.com/felipearocha/Vibration-Accelerated-Corrosion-Coupled-Mechano-Electrochemical-Simulation"
url: "https://github.com/felipearocha/Vibration-Accelerated-Corrosion-Coupled-Mechano-Electrochemical-Simulation"
abstract: >
  Physics-first engineering simulation of vibration-accelerated corrosion in X65 carbon-steel pipe under CO2-saturated brine at low-cycle pipe-support contacts. The model couples four mechanisms: Damped single-degree-of-freedom (SDOF) structural vibration Stress-modified Butler-Volmer electrochemical kinetics (anodic dissolution accelerated by activation-volume term) Faraday mass-loss conversion to corrosion rate Archard fretting wear at support contacts A Gradient-Boosted Regression surrogate is trained on 50,000+ physics-generated data points for real-time deployment. Bonus entry in the Integrity Code Series. Limitations are documented explicitly: stress-activation coefficient is phenomenological, fretting-corrosion synergy term is not modeled, and the pH model uses a Nernst approximation only.
keywords:
  - vibration corrosion
  - mechano-electrochemistry
  - X65 carbon steel
  - CO2 corrosion
  - brine
  - Butler-Volmer
  - stress-modified kinetics
  - SDOF vibration
  - Archard wear
  - fretting
  - surrogate model
  - GBR
  - machine learning surrogate
